1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,006
A guarded aerospace site.

2
00:00:02,356 --> 00:00:08,045
A drone heads in, confirmed about nine
hundred and fifty metres out: in time for

3
00:00:08,045 --> 00:00:08,969
the operator.

4
00:00:09,319 --> 00:00:12,477
What should the screen say when no sensor
sees it?

5
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:17,100
MoVi gives every track one of three
answers.

6
00:00:17,450 --> 00:00:18,495
I see it.

7
00:00:18,845 --> 00:00:21,512
I don't see it: here is where it can be.

8
00:00:21,862 --> 00:00:23,227
Or: I don't know.

9
00:00:23,577 --> 00:00:28,804
In simulation, it says empty only where it
looked, if the site map is right.

10
00:00:29,154 --> 00:00:34,776
A possible-presence warning stays on until
the whole zone is checked, or the object

11
00:00:34,776 --> 00:00:35,724
is seen again.

12
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:43,997
Radar, LiDAR, cameras, aircraft and drone
broadcasts: all simulated from public data

13
00:00:43,997 --> 00:00:44,547
sheets.

14
00:00:44,897 --> 00:00:49,142
Where a sensor cannot see a drone, the
zone stays unverified.

15
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:52,574
Dense fog.

16
00:00:52,924 --> 00:00:55,590
MoVi declares each sensor's reach.

17
00:00:55,940 --> 00:01:01,974
For a small drone, radar range drops from
one thousand and sixty-two to one thousand

18
00:01:01,974 --> 00:01:06,500
and forty-one metres: a small change, not
an independent check.

19
00:01:09,900 --> 00:01:11,650
Two drones collide.

20
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:17,488
MoVi infers the event two point two
seconds later; within two seconds in

21
00:01:17,488 --> 00:01:19,317
fifty-one runs of sixty.

22
00:01:19,667 --> 00:01:21,587
A debris zone opens.

23
00:01:21,937 --> 00:01:26,438
It grows, does not shrink by looking, and
cannot tell who is at risk.

24
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:33,664
An engine fails on take-off, with a flash.

25
00:01:34,014 --> 00:01:39,953
MoVi declares the blinded cameras
unreliable, within three cycles in every

26
00:01:39,953 --> 00:01:41,076
simulated run.

27
00:01:41,426 --> 00:01:47,164
Only the radar is left: here it loses the
aircraft at times, and MoVi says so.

28
00:01:47,514 --> 00:01:52,634
The debris warning does not discriminate:
about ninety-six tracks per run.

29
00:01:53,630 --> 00:01:55,081
First, the limits.

30
00:01:55,431 --> 00:01:58,332
No physical sensor: all simulated.

31
00:01:58,682 --> 00:02:01,434
Almost half the values are assumed.

32
00:02:01,784 --> 00:02:04,174
Classes are labelled by hand.

33
00:02:04,524 --> 00:02:07,766
For aircraft in flight, warnings come too
late.

34
00:02:08,116 --> 00:02:12,980
A drone that stops can slip out of the
warning: twelve runs of two hundred.

35
00:02:13,330 --> 00:02:19,006
What holds, in simulation: a drone on the
site was announced in time in all two

36
00:02:19,006 --> 00:02:24,395
hundred runs, its position never declared
empty, with the site map declared

37
00:02:24,395 --> 00:02:25,042
complete.

38
00:02:29,130 --> 00:02:34,444
The same core, from our short-range
version: a person behind an obstacle, a

39
00:02:34,444 --> 00:02:37,066
depth camera, the same three answers.

40
00:02:39,330 --> 00:02:40,205
MoVi.

41
00:02:40,555 --> 00:02:44,246
Seen, not seen, unknown: declared for
every track.

42
00:02:44,596 --> 00:02:46,729
It observes and warns.

43
00:02:47,079 --> 00:02:49,276
No output is a command.

44
00:02:49,626 --> 00:02:51,674
By SDMs.
